---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="SPDTF"
  description="The SPDTF development workspace: evidence-up modelling, bounded contexts, working groups and reviewable candidates."
>
  <PageMeta category="SPDTF" variant="brand" updated="First collaborative scheme draft · in development" />
  <h1>SPDTF</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    SPDTF is the first Smart Property Data Trust Framework scheme draft being written
    collaboratively across industry and with stakeholders. Its domain-led, evidence-up
    process makes meaning reviewable. It is in development, not yet an adopted standard
    or approved model.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">Development status</p>
    <p>
      Human working groups own domain meaning. Governance controls later promotion. AI
      can extract, compare and draft, but it receives no standards authority. A machine
      validation result proves only the encoded checks, not semantic agreement.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="property-pack">Priority workstream: Property Pack ontology</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/spdtf/property-pack">Property Pack ontology candidate</a> is an
    accelerated component of SPDTF. The Technical Working Group must make an initial
    determination by the end of September 2026; later domain review and controlled change
    remain separate. It is machine-generated, non-normative and not yet determined.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ontology-journey">Semantic modelling</h2>
  <p>
    This journey starts with business questions and keeps semantic meaning distinct from
    validation, projections, implementation and governance. Each page uses the same
    authority contract and links the next reviewable step.
  </p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/ontologies" title="Semantic modelling" description="Follow the complete business-language journey from why ontologies through projections." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/ontologies/semantic-package" title="Six-part semantic package" description="Glossary, dictionary, taxonomies, controlled vocabularies, resources and relationships." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/ontologies/bounded-contexts" title="Bounded contexts and common boundary" description="Keep local precision while making cross-context exchange explicit." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/ontologies/coverage" title="Coverage crosswalk" description="The separate four-lens, 11-theme workshop view and eight formal concerns." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/ontologies/standards" title="Standards, vocabularies and frameworks" description="Targets, candidates and references with bounded conformance and status claims." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/ontologies/evidence-and-mappings" title="Evidence, provenance and mappings" description="Trace claims and distinguish all five mapping meanings." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/candidates" title="Candidate register" description="See whether a context-owned candidate, accountable owner and immutable diff actually exist." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/questions" title="Open questions and changes" description="Reach each group’s competency questions without needing RDF vocabulary." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/outputs" title="Outputs and validation evidence" description="Follow the versioned package manifest and keep projections subordinate to meaning." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/ontologies/validation" title="Validation and generated projections" description="Conformance, lifecycle, receipts and tested downstream representations." />
  </div>

  <h2 id="workspace">Development workspace</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/working-groups" title="Working groups" eyebrow="Canonical workspace" description="The seven named groups plus the peer Interoperability Working Group." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/property-pack" title="Property Pack ontology" eyebrow="Accelerated component" description="Review the 451-item scope, current candidate, September determination and later review path." />
    <GatewayCard href="/governance" title="Governance" eyebrow="Shared service" description="Decision rights, status, lifecycle and promotion records live in one authority tree." />
  </div>
</Layout>
